1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,294
<i>Your father's heart is already recovering.</i>

2
00:00:03,378 --> 00:00:05,672
<i>Now, it seems yours is the one</i>
<i>that needs attention.</i>

3
00:00:07,298 --> 00:00:09,884
<i>- My heart is tough, Auntie.</i>
- [PRECIOUS] <i>Hmm.</i>

4
00:00:10,468 --> 00:00:14,347
<i>Yes, your heart might be tough,</i>
<i>but what about Jordan's heart?</i>

5
00:00:14,431 --> 00:00:15,765
<i>How is he doing?</i>

6
00:00:18,393 --> 00:00:19,561
<i>What about you, Auntie Pres?</i>

7
00:00:19,644 --> 00:00:24,232
<i>Did you notice he had feelings for me?</i>

8
00:00:24,315 --> 00:00:25,692
<i>No, I didn't.</i>

9
00:00:25,775 --> 00:00:30,530
<i>But, Billy, you're both</i>
<i>going through a lot right now.</i>

10
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:34,701
<i>You should be there for each other.</i>

11
00:00:35,827 --> 00:00:38,705
<i>Talk to him. Call him and check on him.</i>

12
00:00:38,788 --> 00:00:41,750
<i>I don't know how to face him right now.</i>

13
00:00:45,086 --> 00:00:46,671
<i>I don't know how.</i>

14
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:51,342
<i>Are you okay now?</i>

15
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:53,636
<i>What I said was true.</i>

16
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:56,139
<i>Since when?</i>

17
00:00:58,558 --> 00:01:01,019
<i>We've grown to know each other</i>
<i>very well, Billy.</i>

18
00:01:05,273 --> 00:01:06,441
<i>Just one look…</i>

19
00:01:08,485 --> 00:01:09,861
<i>and I already know what you're thinking.</i>

20
00:01:12,697 --> 00:01:14,282
<i>I know which smile is real.</i>

21
00:01:16,701 --> 00:01:20,455
<i>I know when you're pissed off</i>
<i>and just pretending to be okay.</i>

22
00:01:23,875 --> 00:01:25,376
<i>I didn't mean to, but…</i>

23
00:01:30,298 --> 00:01:33,051
<i>suddenly, I stopped</i>
<i>memorizing your habits.</i>

24
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:37,222
<i>I started loving them.</i>

25
00:01:43,144 --> 00:01:45,772
<i>I fell in love with all of it.</i>

26
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:50,568
<i>I fell in love with you.</i>

27
00:01:54,239 --> 00:01:56,991
<i>I don't want to ruin what we have.</i>

28
00:02:03,331 --> 00:02:04,582
<i>I couldn't bear it.</i>

29
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:29,149
<i>That might be your last.</i>

30
00:02:31,192 --> 00:02:32,443
<i>I'll take a few days off.</i>

31
00:02:36,072 --> 00:02:37,365
<i>I just need time to…</i>

32
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:41,369
<i>take everything in.</i>

33
00:02:42,704 --> 00:02:44,080
<i>What happened with Dad</i>

34
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:48,167
<i>and your rejection.</i>

35
00:02:49,168 --> 00:02:50,295
<i>Hey!</i>

36
00:03:03,182 --> 00:03:09,439
<i>Is there really no chance</i>
<i>for you to love me again?</i>

37
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:15,486
<i>Mariela…</i>

38
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:19,574
<i>It's time we were good parents to Bea.</i>

39
00:03:20,366 --> 00:03:21,868
<i>That's what matters.</i>

40
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:25,955
<i>So get better. Take care of yourself.</i>

41
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:30,877
[SNIFFLING]

42
00:03:37,759 --> 00:03:38,927
How is she?

43
00:03:39,969 --> 00:03:41,304
Still the same.

44
00:03:41,387 --> 00:03:43,640
She's still being pushy
with what she wants.

45
00:03:44,557 --> 00:03:48,186
She should be grateful she's not in jail.

46
00:03:48,269 --> 00:03:50,605
She committed a huge crime.

47
00:03:50,688 --> 00:03:52,732
- [MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- Crime?

48
00:03:53,358 --> 00:03:56,069
Who do you think is really at fault here?

49
00:03:56,903 --> 00:03:58,821
You're a mistress, Precious.

50
00:03:58,905 --> 00:04:00,823
In the eyes of the law and God,

51
00:04:00,907 --> 00:04:02,992
I'm still the wife.

52
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:04,410
You're just a mistress.

53
00:04:04,494 --> 00:04:07,121
You are the real sinner!

54
00:04:07,205 --> 00:04:08,790
- [SLAPS]
- [NURSE] Police! Police!

55
00:04:08,873 --> 00:04:10,500
- [PRECIOUS GRUNTING]
- [MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

56
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:12,794
- Hey! Stop that!
- Stop it!

57
00:04:13,294 --> 00:04:16,005
You're mine, Enrico! Just mine!

58
00:04:16,714 --> 00:04:17,799
[COP] Come on.

59
00:04:17,882 --> 00:04:19,717
[PRECIOUS BREATHING HEAVILY]

60
00:04:19,801 --> 00:04:21,511
- [COP] Take her to her room.
- Are you okay?

61
00:04:22,553 --> 00:04:29,018
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

62
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:31,271
[MUSIC FADES]

63
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:38,987
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

64
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:39,380
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

65
00:05:39,464 --> 00:05:41,841
Uh, I'm sorry. Bea, right?

66
00:05:41,924 --> 00:05:42,800
Um…

67
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:44,927
You know, you're actually qualified,

68
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:48,014
but I don't think
we'll be able to move forward

69
00:05:48,097 --> 00:05:49,807
with your application.

70
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:52,810
Uh, but why, miss?

71
00:05:52,894 --> 00:05:55,438
My documents are all there.

72
00:05:55,521 --> 00:05:59,192
Well, it shows here that
you have a criminal record.

73
00:05:59,275 --> 00:06:00,610
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:04,489
But that case is over.
It's been settled.

75
00:06:04,572 --> 00:06:07,241
I'm sorry, it's our company policy.

76
00:06:07,325 --> 00:06:09,410
[SCOFFS] "Sorry?"

77
00:06:09,494 --> 00:06:10,745
Company policy, huh?

78
00:06:10,828 --> 00:06:13,498
How can I start over
if you won't give me a chance?

79
00:06:13,581 --> 00:06:15,374
"Policy" my ass!

80
00:06:16,125 --> 00:06:17,251
[SCOFFS]

81
00:06:17,335 --> 00:06:18,961
- What are you looking at?!
- [PHONE RINGING]

82
00:06:23,091 --> 00:06:27,095
[MUSIC TURNS MOROSE]

83
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:28,221
Hello?

84
00:06:35,561 --> 00:06:37,855
What did you do this time?

85
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:39,732
You're making your situation worse.

86
00:06:39,816 --> 00:06:42,110
You shouldn't have done that.

87
00:06:42,193 --> 00:06:44,153
What I did wasn't enough.

88
00:06:44,237 --> 00:06:45,696
Seriously?!

89
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:48,407
I'm trying so hard to win Billy over.

90
00:06:48,491 --> 00:06:50,910
Hurting her Auntie Precious isn't helping!

91
00:06:50,993 --> 00:06:55,039
Ma, please. Can you at least
try to restrain yourself?

92
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:56,415
Try a bit harder, will you?

93
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:59,335
I want to kill your father's mistress!

94
00:06:59,418 --> 00:07:02,130
Seriously?! Could you stop saying that?!

95
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:05,174
Do you really want to get out of here?
Tell me, do you?

96
00:07:05,258 --> 00:07:08,302
Then stop saying you want
to kill people, Ma!

97
00:07:08,386 --> 00:07:10,513
- [BEA SIGHS EXASPERATEDLY] You…
- [KNOCKS ON DOOR]

98
00:07:13,558 --> 00:07:15,643
It's good that you're here, Ms. Mercado.

99
00:07:15,726 --> 00:07:17,478
Uh, can we talk outside?

100
00:07:19,147 --> 00:07:21,274
Okay, I'll be right with you.

101
00:07:25,027 --> 00:07:26,279
Just a moment, Ma.

102
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:30,992
That's good.

103
00:07:32,118 --> 00:07:33,119
Doc.

104
00:07:33,995 --> 00:07:35,163
We've already completed

105
00:07:35,246 --> 00:07:37,290
the second assessment of your mother.

106
00:07:37,373 --> 00:07:39,542
And she has made a huge improvement.

107
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:43,921
She no longer exhibits psychotic symptoms

108
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:46,382
or signs of mental incompetence.

109
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:48,092
She's aware of what she's doing

110
00:07:48,176 --> 00:07:50,678
and the consequences of her actions.

111
00:07:50,761 --> 00:07:54,348
Her previous treatment really helped,

112
00:07:54,432 --> 00:07:57,018
along with the rehabilitation
that she underwent.

113
00:07:57,935 --> 00:08:00,813
Uh, so up to this point,

114
00:08:00,897 --> 00:08:03,191
our evaluation is,

115
00:08:03,274 --> 00:08:05,693
she is already fit to stand trial.

116
00:08:05,776 --> 00:08:08,738
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

117
00:08:08,821 --> 00:08:11,616
What does that mean? What happens now?

118
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:14,660
Once the court order is issued,

119
00:08:15,244 --> 00:08:17,079
we'll put her back in the city jail.

120
00:08:17,705 --> 00:08:19,749
She'll be held there
while her case is ongoing.

121
00:08:21,209 --> 00:08:24,086
Ma'am, that can't be right.
She can't return--

122
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:28,549
Well, we can recommend
continued psychiatric support.

123
00:08:28,633 --> 00:08:30,384
Unfortunately, legally,

124
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:34,096
she does not meet
the criteria for insanity.

125
00:08:36,349 --> 00:08:37,767
All right, we'll get going.

126
00:08:39,352 --> 00:08:46,025
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

127
00:08:46,734 --> 00:08:48,611
[MUSIC FADES]

128
00:08:48,694 --> 00:08:51,656
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

129
00:08:58,329 --> 00:09:05,294
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

130
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:15,846
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

131
00:09:23,813 --> 00:09:24,855
[SHRIEKS]

132
00:09:24,939 --> 00:09:28,484
What? You just suddenly
decide to ghost me?

133
00:09:31,696 --> 00:09:33,447
Dino, I love you,

134
00:09:33,531 --> 00:09:35,825
but I don't want to throw away my life.

135
00:09:37,827 --> 00:09:40,329
The cops just interrogated me.
You're gonna get me in trouble.

136
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:42,164
No one's getting in trouble.

137
00:09:42,748 --> 00:09:45,293
We're leaving. I'll find us a new place.

138
00:09:46,252 --> 00:09:47,253
Look.

139
00:09:48,045 --> 00:09:50,423
See? I have a job now.

140
00:09:51,007 --> 00:09:57,471
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

141
00:09:59,348 --> 00:10:00,558
[MUSIC FADES]

142
00:10:05,521 --> 00:10:08,941
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

143
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:20,244
[PHONE CHIMES]

144
00:10:23,789 --> 00:10:26,917
[WOMAN] <i>Fellow listeners, here it is!</i>
<i>The single you've all been waiting for!</i>

145
00:10:27,001 --> 00:10:29,503
Jordan Valentin's new single,

146
00:10:29,587 --> 00:10:33,382
exclusively on 97.9 LYVE Radio.

147
00:10:33,466 --> 00:10:34,884
"Hurt Me Too."

148
00:10:36,427 --> 00:10:38,262
["HURT ME TOO" PLAYING]

149
00:10:38,346 --> 00:10:42,808
<i>♪ You were always there</i>
<i>When the lights went out ♪</i>

150
00:10:46,062 --> 00:10:49,607
<i>♪ I was there every time you were down ♪</i>

151
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:57,782
<i>♪ We got way too many scars</i>
<i>And it comes with doubt ♪</i>

152
00:10:57,865 --> 00:11:01,202
<i>♪ But what's life</i>
<i>Without a little fighting? ♪</i>

153
00:11:01,285 --> 00:11:04,664
<i>♪ Girl, what's love</i>
<i>Without a little bite? ♪</i>

154
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:08,459
<i>♪ It was way too much and way too fast ♪</i>

155
00:11:08,542 --> 00:11:11,379
<i>♪ I can give you space ♪</i>

156
00:11:12,254 --> 00:11:15,299
<i>♪ But don't be gone too long before ♪</i>

157
00:11:15,383 --> 00:11:17,343
<i>♪ You'll hear me say ♪</i>

158
00:11:17,426 --> 00:11:20,554
<i>♪ I swear, I gave you my best ♪</i>

159
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:24,350
<i>♪ Yeah, I gave it all to you ♪</i>

160
00:11:25,518 --> 00:11:30,898
<i>♪ I know it hurts</i>
<i>Now was it worth the truth? ♪</i>

161
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:34,276
<i>♪ I know you gave me your best ♪</i>

162
00:11:35,528 --> 00:11:38,989
<i>♪ Feels like you're a part of me ♪</i>

163
00:11:39,907 --> 00:11:45,955
<i>♪ I know it hurts</i>
<i>'Cause that shit hurt me too ♪</i>

164
00:11:46,038 --> 00:11:50,334
<i>♪ Oh, even all the greatest stories end ♪</i>

165
00:11:50,918 --> 00:11:53,587
<i>♪ And I would do it all again ♪</i>

166
00:11:54,296 --> 00:11:56,424
<i>♪ I know it hurts ♪</i>

167
00:11:57,716 --> 00:12:03,556
<i>♪ Ain't nothing worse than losing you ♪</i>

168
00:12:05,266 --> 00:12:06,851
<i>♪ Mm ♪</i>

169
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:10,479
<i>♪ Than losing you ♪</i>

170
00:12:11,689 --> 00:12:13,691
<i>♪ Oh ♪</i>

171
00:12:15,192 --> 00:12:18,362
<i>♪ Than losing you ♪</i>

172
00:12:20,448 --> 00:12:22,199
[MUSIC ENDS]

173
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:24,660
- [ROBBIE] Wow!
- [CHEERING]

174
00:12:25,327 --> 00:12:27,371
[FANS AND ROBBIE CHANTING]
<i>Jordan! Jordan!</i>

175
00:12:27,455 --> 00:12:31,167
Jordan! Jordan! Jordan!

176
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:37,006
[CHEERING]

177
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:41,844
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

178
00:12:41,927 --> 00:12:43,387
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER,
FANS SQUEALING]

179
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:44,972
[ROBBIE] All right,
take your pictures now.

180
00:12:45,055 --> 00:12:46,348
Hurry up! Come on!

181
00:12:46,432 --> 00:12:47,600
- [SHUTTERS CLICKING]
- Hey!

182
00:12:47,683 --> 00:12:49,435
[SECURITY] Hey, let's move
over there, please.

183
00:12:49,518 --> 00:12:51,312
[ROBBIE] That's enough for now!

184
00:12:51,395 --> 00:12:52,980
Let's move to the other hallway, please.

185
00:12:53,063 --> 00:12:56,025
- Please wait over there.
- [FANS, OVERLAPPING] Bye, Jordan!

186
00:12:56,108 --> 00:12:57,693
- This way, please.
- Bye, Jordan!

187
00:12:57,776 --> 00:12:59,904
Bye! Bye, Jordan!

188
00:12:59,987 --> 00:13:01,155
Bye!

189
00:13:01,238 --> 00:13:04,909
Wow! Boss, you've really leveled up!

190
00:13:04,992 --> 00:13:07,495
Look at that. All those girls
are going crazy over you!

191
00:13:08,496 --> 00:13:11,373
Meanwhile, I'm still trying
to find someone on LoveList.

192
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:13,334
- Really?
- Yeah. I matched with someone.

193
00:13:13,417 --> 00:13:15,211
We went on a date.

194
00:13:15,294 --> 00:13:16,462
Then she blocked me.

195
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:20,341
Maybe she just wasn't the one for you.

196
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:22,343
You know, take it easy.

197
00:13:22,968 --> 00:13:24,303
You'll find the right one.

198
00:13:25,429 --> 00:13:26,889
Do you really believe that, boss?

199
00:13:26,972 --> 00:13:28,599
That whole "take it easy" thing?

200
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:31,101
You took it way too easy yourself,
and you lost the one for you.

201
00:13:33,062 --> 00:13:35,981
Billy said she wants to
keep our friendship.

202
00:13:36,732 --> 00:13:37,900
And I agree.

203
00:13:38,526 --> 00:13:43,656
You know, sometimes,
friendship lasts longer.

204
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:49,036
Well…

205
00:13:49,828 --> 00:13:51,288
Take it easy, boss.

206
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:54,166
You'll find the right one.

207
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:57,711
Yeah, yeah. I'll press it now.

208
00:13:57,795 --> 00:13:59,213
This elevator's taking forever.

209
00:13:59,296 --> 00:14:02,049
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

210
00:14:03,759 --> 00:14:07,555
I'll expedite Mariela's clinical diagnosis

211
00:14:08,389 --> 00:14:10,599
so I can submit it to the court.

212
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:15,062
I think it'll give us strong grounds
for getting our marriage annulled.

213
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:17,147
And what about you abandoning them?

214
00:14:18,023 --> 00:14:19,942
That's probably for the best for everyone.

215
00:14:21,652 --> 00:14:23,904
I actually think it might be better if

216
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:28,492
I stayed with Bea
until our marriage is annulled.

217
00:14:30,286 --> 00:14:31,620
I understand.

218
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:34,874
You have to be there
for your other daughter too.

219
00:14:34,957 --> 00:14:37,459
I'm just worried about your health.

220
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:40,379
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

221
00:14:40,462 --> 00:14:42,172
I'll take care of myself.

222
00:14:43,757 --> 00:14:45,342
- [BILLY] Dad?
- [KNOCKS]

223
00:14:49,179 --> 00:14:50,389
Auntie?

224
00:14:52,182 --> 00:14:53,350
What happened to your face?

225
00:14:53,434 --> 00:14:56,937
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

226
00:14:57,479 --> 00:14:59,189
Exactly, Attorney. That's what I'm saying.

227
00:14:59,273 --> 00:15:00,566
Fine, my mother was wrong.

228
00:15:00,649 --> 00:15:04,028
But I've already talked to her about it.
She won't do it again.

229
00:15:04,111 --> 00:15:07,239
Your mother's case is getting worse, Bea.

230
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:10,951
Considering the circumstances
and her behavior,

231
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:13,203
It'll be difficult to get her out of jail.

232
00:15:13,287 --> 00:15:15,331
So that's it? We just let it happen?

233
00:15:15,414 --> 00:15:17,666
Is there really nothing we can do?

234
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:21,378
Again, we can try to reach
a settlement with Ms. Cariño.

235
00:15:21,462 --> 00:15:24,506
<i>And that could resolve</i>
<i>the civil aspect of the case.</i>

236
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:27,217
<i>But as for the criminal charges, even if</i>

237
00:15:27,301 --> 00:15:28,886
the Cariños withdraw their complaint,

238
00:15:28,969 --> 00:15:31,722
the state can still pursue the case.

239
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:33,182
[HUFFS]

240
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:40,022
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

241
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:45,110
<i>Billy.</i>

242
00:15:46,862 --> 00:15:48,155
<i>Billy, I'm begging you.</i>

243
00:15:48,238 --> 00:15:51,408
<i>If you drop the case against my mom,</i>

244
00:15:51,492 --> 00:15:54,119
<i>I promise I'll watch over her.</i>

245
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:56,664
<i>I promise she won't bother you.</i>

246
00:15:56,747 --> 00:16:01,043
<i>I promise, Billy. Please.</i>
<i>Just withdraw the case against my mother.</i>

247
00:16:01,126 --> 00:16:02,461
<i>Please, Billy. Please.</i>

248
00:16:02,544 --> 00:16:04,463
<i>Have mercy on my mother. Please.</i>

249
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:07,091
<i>If you were in my position,</i>

250
00:16:09,009 --> 00:16:13,138
<i>and your family had almost died</i>
<i>because of someone…</i>

251
00:16:15,975 --> 00:16:18,060
<i>would you really let her walk free?</i>

252
00:16:18,143 --> 00:16:25,025
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

253
00:16:30,823 --> 00:16:32,074
Oh.

254
00:16:33,742 --> 00:16:35,661
I'll stay with your sister Bea
for a while, okay?

255
00:16:36,912 --> 00:16:38,497
I'm going to miss you, Papa.

256
00:16:39,248 --> 00:16:40,416
I'll miss you too.

257
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:42,584
- [OLIVER] Love you.
- [ENRICO] Love you.

258
00:16:42,668 --> 00:16:43,836
I love you.

259
00:16:43,919 --> 00:16:45,879
- [ENRICO LAUGHS] I love you.
- I love you.

260
00:16:47,131 --> 00:16:49,591
We'll still see each other every day.

261
00:16:49,675 --> 00:16:53,178
I'll be waiting for you at the gate
first thing in the morning.

262
00:16:53,262 --> 00:16:56,432
We'll spend recess
and lunch together, okay?

263
00:16:57,016 --> 00:16:57,850
Yes, Pa.

264
00:16:57,933 --> 00:17:00,019
Enrico, remember that
we're always here for you.

265
00:17:00,644 --> 00:17:02,688
By the way, is Billy here?

266
00:17:02,771 --> 00:17:04,023
I want to say goodbye to her.

267
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:06,150
I'll call her.

268
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:10,946
Billy?

269
00:17:20,247 --> 00:17:23,000
- [LINE RINGS]
- Billy, where are you?

270
00:17:23,083 --> 00:17:25,002
I'm just going to talk to Bea.

271
00:17:25,586 --> 00:17:27,713
- Billy…
<i>- This is about her mother.</i>

272
00:17:28,672 --> 00:17:32,384
This is exactly why that woman
can't be allowed to go free.

273
00:17:33,677 --> 00:17:34,678
Billy, dear?

274
00:17:36,847 --> 00:17:38,557
[CALL ENDS]

275
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:44,021
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

276
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:04,416
[BEA] <i>We need to figure out</i>

277
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:07,294
<i>how to break her out of that hospital.</i>

278
00:18:07,377 --> 00:18:10,130
<i>The problem is, it's not easy.</i>

279
00:18:10,214 --> 00:18:13,550
<i>Planning it will be hard, especially since</i>
<i>they're about to send her back to prison.</i>

280
00:18:13,634 --> 00:18:15,719
[CALOY] <i>Come here.</i>
<i>Stop worrying about it.</i>

281
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:18,430
<i>Just relax for a while.</i>

282
00:18:18,514 --> 00:18:20,474
<i>Let's have a drink.</i>

283
00:18:21,058 --> 00:18:24,394
<i>What are you talking about?</i>
<i>I didn't come here to drink with you.</i>

284
00:18:24,478 --> 00:18:26,814
<i>Caloy, help my mother.</i>

285
00:18:26,897 --> 00:18:27,981
[CALOY SIGHS]

286
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:30,067
[CALOY] <i>Don't worry, okay?</i>

287
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:31,944
<i>I'll take care of everything.</i>

288
00:18:34,655 --> 00:18:36,824
<i>We'll break your mother out.</i>

289
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:40,452
<i>You know I'd do anything for you, right?</i>

290
00:18:42,454 --> 00:18:45,999
<i>Because I love you so much.</i>

291
00:18:52,089 --> 00:18:54,508
<i>Fine! I love you too.</i>

292
00:18:59,429 --> 00:19:01,098
<i>Don't you dare mess with me!</i>

293
00:19:03,183 --> 00:19:05,394
<i>I'll make sure you go back</i>
<i>to prison, you witch.</i>

294
00:19:05,477 --> 00:19:06,687
<i>- Billy!</i>
<i>- What?!</i>

295
00:19:06,770 --> 00:19:08,063
<i>Billy, that's enough!</i>

296
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:09,731
<i>Your sister already explained everything.</i>

297
00:19:10,816 --> 00:19:12,276
<i>I'll deal with Bea.</i>

298
00:19:13,193 --> 00:19:14,444
<i>Seriously?</i>

299
00:19:16,029 --> 00:19:19,408
<i>Are you seriously taking</i>
<i>that woman's side?</i>

300
00:19:20,993 --> 00:19:22,786
<i>The proof is right here!</i>

301
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:24,204
<i>Fine.</i>

302
00:19:24,288 --> 00:19:26,748
<i>Then you and your daughter</i>
<i>can stick together.</i>

303
00:19:33,839 --> 00:19:36,133
<i>Billy, your father's</i>
<i>in a difficult position.</i>

304
00:19:36,216 --> 00:19:37,759
<i>He's caught in the middle.</i>

305
00:19:37,843 --> 00:19:40,470
<i>You're both his children,</i>
<i>and he loves you both.</i>

306
00:19:40,554 --> 00:19:41,889
<i>We're both his children,</i>

307
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:44,141
<i>but only one of us is a criminal.</i>

308
00:19:44,224 --> 00:19:48,353
<i>Maybe your father feels that</i>
<i>he's partly to blame</i>

309
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:50,606
<i>for Bea turning out this way.</i>

310
00:19:50,689 --> 00:19:53,192
<i>Bea can think for herself, Auntie.</i>

311
00:19:53,275 --> 00:19:56,111
<i>Everything she does,</i>
<i>every decision she makes,</i>

312
00:19:56,195 --> 00:19:58,739
<i>is her own choice, not anyone else's.</i>

313
00:19:58,822 --> 00:20:02,284
<i>Even conspiring with Caloy</i>
<i>is her decision.</i>

314
00:20:02,367 --> 00:20:05,704
<i>So if that man causes trouble</i>
<i>for our family again,</i>

315
00:20:05,787 --> 00:20:08,207
<i>Bea will be to blame for it.</i>

316
00:20:08,790 --> 00:20:10,542
<i>You shouldn't have done that!</i>

317
00:20:11,126 --> 00:20:13,629
<i>It's dangerous to have</i>
<i>any contact with that man!</i>

318
00:20:13,712 --> 00:20:14,671
<i>I know, Pa.</i>

319
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:17,341
<i>But like I said earlier,</i>
<i>I did it to protect you.</i>

320
00:20:17,424 --> 00:20:22,054
<i>I wanted to protect my half-siblings too,</i>
<i>and Auntie Precious.</i>

321
00:20:22,137 --> 00:20:23,388
<i>That's all, Pa.</i>

322
00:20:23,472 --> 00:20:24,973
<i>Just stay here. I'll figure something out.</i>

323
00:20:25,057 --> 00:20:26,433
<i>Make sure you do, okay?</i>

324
00:20:26,516 --> 00:20:30,354
<i>Because Billy won't listen</i>
<i>to me anymore, Caloy.</i>

325
00:20:30,437 --> 00:20:33,065
<i>Even if I begged on my knees,</i>

326
00:20:33,148 --> 00:20:36,026
<i>she wouldn't change her mind.</i>
